# MUCHI — Workers Static Assets header rules.
#
# IMPORTANT: Workers applies ALL matching rules to a request (values are
# appended into one Cache-Control header), and when both are present
# `no-store` wins over `public`. So the app shell files that the service
# worker must always revalidate (html/js/css) get an explicit no-store rule,
# while everything else (images, manifest) gets public caching.
#
#   .html/.js/.css (+ /)  -> no-store (the service worker always gets fresh copies)
#   everything else       -> public, max-age=86400

/
  Cache-Control: no-store, max-age=0

/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-store, max-age=0

/*.js
  Cache-Control: no-store, max-age=0

/*.css
  Cache-Control: no-store, max-age=0

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
